# Copy to .env.local (dev) or .env.production (build). Only VITE_-prefixed vars
# reach the browser, and Vite inlines them at BUILD time — a missing value is
# baked in as a dead placeholder rather than failing loudly.
#
# ── truhq.co (the marketing site, Pages project `tru-landing`) ───────────────
# Set ONLY VITE_WORKER_URL. Leave the two Supabase vars unset, deliberately:
#
#   App.tsx renders the marketing home whenever there is no session. With real
#   Supabase credentials a signed-in visitor to truhq.co would get the PRODUCT
#   shell instead of the marketing page — and this branch's copy of the product
#   is far behind main, so they would see a stale one. Without credentials the
#   session always resolves to null and truhq.co is always the marketing site,
#   which is what we want.
#
# ── app.truhq.co (the product, Pages project `tru-pulse-app`) ────────────────
# Needs ALL THREE, built from `main`. The real values live in
# truhq/pulse/web/.env.production, which is gitignored — copy it in before
# building or login ships pointed at a host that does not exist.
#
# Verify any app build before promoting it:
#   grep -c yeyoteredgunhvhqmais dist/assets/*.js   # must be >= 1
#   grep -c demo.supabase.co     dist/assets/*.js   # must be 0

VITE_SUPABASE_URL=https://<project>.supabase.co
VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=<supabase anon key>
VITE_WORKER_URL=https://tru-pulse-sync.<your-account>.workers.dev
